; OBJVERIF3 - OBJVERIF plus more unreachable prose (MTX 28-87) so ndrc -nxtext
; picks the 383-token alphabet; every reachable text and the walk are unchanged.
;
; OBJVERIF - compressed object texts and shared duplicate texts.
;
; BLANK_EN template shape (DAAD V2, English). Plain DAAD condacts only,
; 7-bit ASCII text, so it compiles for NEXTDAAD and the classic targets.
;
; Stimuli (byte-asserted by assert_stim.py):
;   object texts carrying token references: one starting with a token,
;   one ending with one, one a single token, one holding a 12-byte token;
;   articles "a lamp", "the key", "some coins";
;   '_' messages (EXAMINE, SM36-SM39) and one '@' message;
;   duplicate pairs: OTX 0/7, STX 63/64, MTX 23/24, LTX 1/2, empty MTX 25/26.
; Window is 32x10 so More... fires inside the inventory list.

#define fDark               0
#define fObjectsCarried     1
#define fDarkF              28
#define fGFlags             29
#define fScore              30
#define fTurns              31
#define fTurnsHi            32
#define fVerb               33
#define fNoun               34
#define fAdject1            35
#define fAdverb             36
#define fMaxCarr            37
#define fPlayer             38
#define fPrep               43
#define fNoun2              44
#define fAdject2            45
#define fCPronounNoun       46
#define fCPronounAdject     47
#define fTimeout            48
#define fTimeoutFlags       49
#define fDoallObjNo         50
#define fRefObject          51
#define fStrength           52
#define fObjFlags           53

#define TIMEOUT   87


/CTL
_


;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/VOC

N       2       noun
NORTH   2       noun
S       3       noun
SOUTH   3       noun

I       14      noun
INVEN   14      noun

LAMP    50      noun
KEY     51      noun
COINS   52      noun
MAP     53      noun
SCROL   54      noun
CLOAK   55      noun
RING    56      noun
LANTE   57      noun

GET     20      verb
TAKE    20      verb
DROP    21      verb
REMOV   22      verb
WEAR    23      verb
LOOK    30      verb
L       30      verb
EXAMI   32      verb
X       32      verb
PAIRS   33      verb
EMPTY   34      verb
TEST    35      verb

AND     2       conjugation
THEN    2       conjugation


;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/STX
/0 "It's too dark to see anything."
/1 "I can also see: "
/2 "#nWhat now?"
/3 "#nWhat next?"
/4 "#nWhat should I do now?"
/5 "#nWhat should I do next?"
/6 "#nI was not able to understand any of that.  Please try again."
/7 "#nI can't go in that direction."
/8 "I can't do that.#n"
/9 "I have with me:#n"
/10 "I am wearing:#n"
/11 ""
/12 "Are you sure? "
/13 "Would you like another go? "
/14 ""
/15 "OK.#n"
/16 "Press any key to continue.#n"
/17 ""
/18 ""
/19 ""
/20 ""
/21 ""
/22 ""
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those.#n"
/24 "I can't.  I'm wearing the _."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 "#n>"
/34 ""
/35 "#nTime passes...#n"
/36 "I now have the _.#n"
/37 "I'm now wearing the _.#n"
/38 "I've removed the _.#n"
/39 "I've dropped the _.#n"
/40 "I can't wear the _.#n"
/41 "I can't remove the _.#n"
/42 "I can't remove the _.  My hands are full.#n"
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me.#n"
/44 "#nThe _ is in the "
/45 "The _ isn't in the "
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _.#n"
/50 "I'm not wearing the _.#n"
/51 ".#n"
/52 "There isn't one of those in the "
/53 "Nothing.#n"
/54 "T"
/55 "D"
/56 "Drive not ready - press any key to retry.#n"
/57 "I/O Error.#n"
/58 "Disc or Directory may be full."
/59 "Invalid filename."
/60 "Type in name of file:"
/61 "Start tape.#n"
/62 "Tape or Disc?"
/63 "SM pair: this system text is stored once.#n"
/64 "SM pair: this system text is stored once.#n"


;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/MTX
/0 ""
/1 "OBJVERIF - compressed object texts."
/2 "You examine _ closely."
/3 "@ is here, with some coins."
/4 "It is a lamp. Not the key, not some coins, just a lamp."
/5 "It is the key. Not a lamp, not some coins, just the key."
/6 "It is some coins. Not a lamp, not the key, just some coins."
/7 "The map shows the course of the winding river valley."
/8 "The scroll is sealed by the old king."
/9 "The cloak with a frayed hem is warm."
/10 "The ring bears the seal of the old king."
/11 "A second lamp, the twin of a lamp."
/12 "Some coins, the key and a lamp lie by the winding river valley."
/13 "The old king hid some coins and the key in the winding river valley."
/14 "Look for a lamp, the key and some coins."
/15 "Then a lamp, then the key, then some coins."
/16 "First the winding river valley, then the old king."
/17 "Sysmess pair:"
/18 "Message pair:"
/19 "Empty pair follows:"
/20 "Empty pair done."
/21 "Location pair:"
/22 "Pairs done."
/23 "MTX pair: this message text is stored once."
/24 "MTX pair: this message text is stored once."
/25 ""
/26 ""
/27 "Location number "
/28 "The river bends east below the old mill, where the water runs slow and brown over the stones."
/29 "A narrow path climbs from the valley floor through a wood of beech and holly towards the ridge."
/30 "Rain has fallen all night and the track is soft underfoot, the ruts filled with cold grey water."
/31 "Beyond the gate the fields open out, green and wet, with a line of willows marking the stream."
/32 "The farmhouse stands empty, its shutters closed and its chimney cold, the yard grown over with nettles."
/33 "From the top of the hill you can see the whole valley laid out below, the river shining in the sun."
/34 "An old stone bridge crosses the water here, its arches low and its parapet worn smooth by many hands."
/35 "The wind comes down from the moor in long gusts, bending the grass and rattling the dry bracken."
/36 "A heron stands motionless in the shallows, watching the water for the flicker of a passing fish."
/37 "The lane runs between high hedges thick with bramble, and the smell of wet earth hangs in the air."
/38 "Smoke rises from a cottage in the trees, and somewhere a dog is barking at the edge of the wood."
/39 "The church tower stands above the village roofs, its clock stopped at a quarter past some old hour."
/40 "Under the trees the light is green and dim, and the only sound is the drip of water from the leaves."
/41 "A long wall of dry stone follows the slope of the hill, broken here and there where sheep have pushed through."
/42 "The mill race is silent now, its wheel rotted and still, the water turned aside into the old channel."
/43 "Mist lies along the valley in the early morning, and the far bank of the river is lost in grey."
/44 "The road is older than the village and older than the church, and nobody can say who first laid it."
/45 "In the orchard the apples have fallen and lie rotting in the grass, and wasps drift lazily between them."
/46 "The inn sign creaks on its iron bracket, the painted swan faded almost to nothing by sun and rain."
/47 "A cart track leads off to the north, rutted and overgrown, towards the quarry on the far side of the hill."
/48 "The river bends east below the old mill, where the water runs slow and brown over the stones. A heron stands motionless in the shallows, watching the water for the flicker of a passing fish."
